      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "on Intel-tactics PDFMLC reported F1 70.93% and recall 81.48% vs\nbaselines (deep forest, random forest, extra trees, rcATT). On benchmark\ndatasets PDFMLC outperformed deep forest (example: enron 70.24% vs\n68.38%). Parallelization achieved speedups up to 4.65 (yeast); mutual-\ninformation thresholding showed many MI values in 0–0.1 and dataset-\nspecific optimal t. Case study: Hogfish reports merged and converted to\nSTIX2.1 tactic tags (e.g., TA0002). Experimental cluster and parameters\nlisted.",
      "fontSize": 13.182547426104794,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "on Intel-tactics PDFMLC reported F1 70.93% and recall 81.48% vs baselines (deep forest, random forest, extra trees, rcATT). On benchmark datasets PDFMLC outperformed deep forest (example: enron 70.24% vs 68.38%). Parallelization achieved speedups up to 4.65 (yeast); mutual-information thresholding showed many MI values in 0–0.1 and dataset-specific optimal t. Case study: Hogfish reports merged and converted to STIX2.1 tactic tags (e.g., TA0002). Experimental cluster and parameters listed.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "F8w6AgNyi1AxQaUcDCA8h",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10991.84529832011,
      "y": 1499.8419417344396,
      "width": 447.6502952739607,
      "height": 82.39092141315496,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4wb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1401710624,
      "version": 913,
      "versionNonce": 444011235,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760343500663,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "text-extraction artifacts propagate and degrade downstream results; some\nclasses (campaign, tool) have low recall because they are often implicit; KB\nrequires curation to avoid drift; rcATT classifier may need more\ndata/reparameterization. Authors release dataset and some code for\nreproducibility.",
      "fontSize": 13.182547426104794,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "text-extraction artifacts propagate and degrade downstream results; some classes (campaign, tool) have low recall because they are often implicit; KB requires curation to avoid drift; rcATT classifier may need more data/reparameterization. Authors release dataset and some code for reproducibility.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hk24fZzVgtWX_-lNa47Vy",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10379.221130053358,
      "y": 1535.2161080224082,
      "width": 447.6502952739607,
      "height": 65.91273713052398,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4wc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1949575200,
      "version": 1031,
      "versionNonce": 734282208,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760297680792,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "focus limited to tactics (techniques and procedures not automated);\nparallel speedup depends on dataset size (smaller datasets show less\nbenefit); LZW/broadcast strategy and hyperparameters require tuning;\nfuture work listed to extend to full TTP extraction and deeper parallelism.",
      "fontSize": 13.182547426104794,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "focus limited to tactics (techniques and procedures not automated); parallel speedup depends on dataset size (smaller datasets show less benefit); LZW/broadcast strategy and hyperparameters require tuning; future work listed to extend to full TTP extraction and deeper parallelism.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "UY7l21WeJYYyHEPpHDaPN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10990.32398076973,
      "y": 1192.6448881149747,
      "width": 448.35443451167566,
      "height": 148.30365854367895,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4wd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1586566176,
      "version": 804,
      "versionNonce": 1148763779,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760343500663,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "pipeline with Text Extraction (Apache Tika / ConvertAPI and cleaning),\nEntity Extraction via four independent submodules (IOC regex finder,\nKnowledge-Base string lookup with Aho-Corasick + POS filtering, novel-\nentity detection via spaCy dependency/POS patterns, and a retrained rcATT\nmulti-label TTP classifier), Relation Extraction via two submodules\n(shortest-dependency-path rule mapping and SBERT-style sentence-\nembedding similarity with cosine threshold 0.5), then confidence-based\nmerge and STIX-2.1 JSON output plus GUI. Modules are plug-and-play and\nKB is interactive.",
      "fontSize": 13.182547426104792,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "pipeline with Text Extraction (Apache Tika / ConvertAPI and cleaning), Entity Extraction via four independent submodules (IOC regex finder, Knowledge-Base string lookup with Aho-Corasick + POS filtering, novel-entity detection via spaCy dependency/POS patterns, and a retrained rcATT multi-label TTP classifier), Relation Extraction via two submodules (shortest-dependency-path rule mapping and SBERT-style sentence-embedding similarity with cosine threshold 0.5), then confidence-based merge and STIX-2.1 JSON output plus GUI. Modules are plug-and-play and KB is interactive.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-GQ0xLs5CSdjEFxdLtIH0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 10377.699812502979,
      "y": 1203.628619811897,
      "width": 448.35443451167566,
      "height": 164.7818428263099,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dashed",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4wh",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 916056544,
      "version": 856,
      "versionNonce": 318852128,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1760297680792,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "build Intel-tactics dataset (~12,900 scraped reports, annotated into\nATT&CK-aligned tactic classes); PDFMLC combines a parallel Multi-\nGrained Scan (sliding-window feature expansion) and a parallel Cascade\nForest trained on Spark. To reduce network cost PDFMLC compresses\nsliding-window outputs with LZW and broadcasts them as variables to\nworker nodes. It computes label mutual information I(X;Y), selects pairs\nabove threshold t to form an MI feature vector M, and concatenates M with\nmulti-grained vector S and cascade vector V through layers. Input features\nare TF-IDF text vectors. Algorithms and time-complexity formulas are\nprovided",
      "fontSize": 13.182547426104792,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "build Intel-tactics dataset (~12,900 scraped reports, annotated into ATT&CK-aligned tactic classes); PDFMLC combines a parallel Multi-Grained Scan (sliding-window feature expansion) and a parallel Cascade Forest trained on Spark. To reduce network cost PDFMLC compresses sliding-window outputs with LZW and broadcasts them as variables to worker nodes. It computes label mutual information I(X;Y), selects pairs above threshold t to form an MI feature vector M, and concatenates M with multi-grained vector S and cascade vector V through layers. Input features are TF-IDF text vectors. Algorithms and time-complexity formulas are provided",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
